  "composite_prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept.\nAsset type: S07 riverside gathering scene, DAY complete original composite C for a quiet game.\nInput Image 1 is STYLE REFERENCE ONLY. Match its coarse visible gouache strokes, dry-brush edges, colored-pencil contour marks, sparse forms and muted matte palette. Do not reproduce the indoor subject.\nScene: a riverside footpath at the edge of a small town in soft diffuse morning daylight. A simple low stone arch bridge crosses the narrow river in the left background. A broad bare earth footpath curves along the left bank. One clearly structured plain tree trunk rises at the far-left edge with a single readable sage canopy extending across the upper-left. A few simple foreground grass tufts along the left riverbank, one restrained clump of tiny wildflowers, and a small cluster of three pale quartz stones among moss beside the path. Keep these few objects readable and separate.\nComposition: 16:9 wide edge-to-edge. River bend, path and bridge occupy the left two thirds; rightmost 30 percent is smooth quiet dusty-teal river surface with only a few broad horizontal brush marks and a low distant bank. Bottom 12 percent mainly plain ground and quiet water, with the few foreground grass tufts near lower-left only. Soft modest sky; no houses in view, people, boats, animals, lamps, ornamental structures or dense foliage clutter. Water is matte paint, not photorealistic reflection.\nSTYLE_V2: gouache picture-book illustration, visible brush strokes and dry-brush edges, slightly wobbly hand-drawn colored-pencil outlines, simplified shapes, slightly imperfect perspective, limited palette of seven muted colors (cream, warm grey, walnut brown, sage green, dusty teal, faded plum, ochre), soft diffuse daylight, cool-tinted shadows, generous empty wall and floor space interpreted here as generous quiet open bank and water, only a few props, one clear focal point, calm and quiet, matte paper texture, no text, no people.\nNEGATIVE: glow, bloom, light rays, god rays, lens flare, bokeh, depth of field blur, gold filigree, ornate carvings, glossy or plastic surfaces, hyper-detailed clutter, photorealism, symmetrical fantasy composition, wisteria everywhere, text, letters, numbers, UI, labels, blank plaques, interface frames, borders.\nRequested native 2560×1440 if available, otherwise actual largest native 16:9. Do not draw resolution text.",
  "cleanplate_prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit.\nAsset type: S07 DAY raw cleanplate B_all for true extracted foreground grass and tree-canopy layers.\nInput Image 1 is the exact EDIT TARGET. Remove ONLY the following:\n1. All leaves of the foreground tree canopy across the upper-left/top edge. Keep the main tree trunk and thick bare branch structure in their original positions and fill behind removed leaves with the original painted sky.\n2. The foreground grass tufts along the lower-left riverbank and beside the curving path, including the small wildflower stalks that grow among those tufts. Fill behind them with the plausible plain earth path/bank or water immediately behind the specific blades.\nKeep the three pale stones and their moss, the static tree trunk/branches, bridge masonry, every riverbank boundary, background distant vegetation, path position and sky/clouds unchanged. IMPORTANT: retain the water itself and its existing painted brush marks; do not erase the river, replace it with land, or invent water waves. Water will later use an exact region mask from this original composite, not a regenerated ripple image.\nKeep DAY lighting, color, camera, crop and same native dimensions; preserve unrelated pixels as closely as possible. Maintain the matte gouache medium, visible dry-brush strokes, slightly wobbly colored-pencil outline and muted seven-family palette.\nNo new objects, people, animals, text, numbers, UI, plaques, borders, glow, bloom, bright sparkles or photorealism.",
  "annotation_notes": "Manual native-pixel polygons inspected against the actual same-composition C; each period/state retains its own C/raw B; no independently redrawn Li.",
